Playing as a human rogue, I had a pretty solid game going.  I was
level 12, down to -10 AC, got poison, sleep, cold resistance and a
luckstone.  I had gauntlets of power but no other magic armor except
an elven cloak.  No magic resistance or reflection yet (bag of holding
in Sokoban), but I figured that wouldn't be a problem as long as I
stayed out of Fort Ludios and found some before Medusa.  On the Rogue
level I accidentally stumbled into my quest portal, and even though I
wasn't 14 yet I figured I'd take a look around.  I was walking around
without a light, fighting off nymphs, leprechauns, chameleons, easily
killing anything I came across.  In the middle of one of the dark
rooms I walked into a monster and suddenly saw "Do you want your items
identified?".  I looked back and saw "The arch-lich hits!  Oh no, he's
using the touch of death!"

Now I don't KNOW that it was a chameleon, but I'm pretty sure arch-
liches don't just hang out on the first floor of the quest level.

So let this be a lesson, if you don't have magic resistance, you are
not safe :P  Also, I guess something about carrying proper lighting
equipment?

